<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Mean price claim</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>{@nm@} mixes \({@m1@}\) kg of maize flour at Ksh \({@p1@}\) a kilogram with \({@m2@}\) kg of {@fl@} flour at Ksh \({@p2@}\) a kilogram to make uji flour, and says: <q>The mixture costs \(({@p1@} + {@p2@}) \div 2 = {@dd(mn)@}\) shillings a kilogram.</q></p><p>(a) Which statement is right?</p><p>[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p><p>(b) What does 1 kg of the mixture cost, to the nearest shilling?</p><p>Ksh [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</p><p>(c) Keeping the \({@m1@}\) kg of maize flour, how many kilograms of {@fl@} flour would make {@nm@}'s statement true?</p><p>[[input:ans3]] kg [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</p>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>(a) and (b) Total cost: \({@m1@} \times {@p1@} + {@m2@} \times {@p2@} = {@ksh(tc)@}\) shillings. Total mass: \({@m1+m2@}\) kg. Cost of 1 kg: \({@ksh(tc)@} \div {@m1+m2@} [[if test="is(integerp(100*cc))"]]= {@ksh(cc)@}[[else]]\approx {@ksh(cc)@}[[/if]]\), so Ksh \({@floor(cc+1/2)@}\) to the nearest shilling. The cost of a mixture leans towards the ingredient you use more of: here {@mw@}.</p><p>(c) The mean of the prices is right only when the two masses are equal, so \({@m1@}\) kg of {@fl@} flour. Check: \(({@m1@} \times {@p1@} + {@m1@} \times {@p2@}) \div {@2*m1@} = {@dd(mn)@}\).</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>3</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
  <idnumber></idnumber>
  <stackversion><text>2026063000</text></stackversion>
  <questionvariables>
    <text><![CDATA[kgrp(n) := block([s, out, k], s: string(n), k: slength(s), if k < 5 then s else (out: "", while k > 3 do (out: sconcat("\\,", substring(s, k-2, k+1), out), k: k-3), sconcat(substring(s, 1, k+1), out)));
ksh(v) := block([c, w, f], c: floor(100*v+1/2), w: floor(c/100), f: c-100*w, if f = 0 then kgrp(w) else sconcat(kgrp(w), ".", if f < 10 then "0" else "", string(f)));
dd(v) := if integerp(v) then v else if integerp(10*v) then dispdp(float(v),1) else if integerp(100*v) then dispdp(float(v),2) else if integerp(1000*v) then dispdp(float(v),3) else dispdp(float(v),4);
fr(v) := if integerp(v) then string(v) else sconcat("\\frac{", string(num(v)), "}{", string(denom(v)), "}");
r1(v) := floor(10*v+1/2)/10;
ix: 1+rand(10);
/* Design: claim pattern. Source: original. [m1, p1, m2, p2, flour, order]: m1 kg maize flour at p1 with m2 kg of a second flour at p2 (more of the cheaper flour in 5 entries, more of the dearer in 5), and the option display order (correct never first). Curated list, one seed per entry. */
L: [[6,70,2,225,"millet",[4,3,1,2]],[3,68,5,180,"millet",[1,4,2,3]],[8,72,2,150,"sorghum",[3,2,1,4]],[2,66,6,210,"millet",[1,3,4,2]],[5,74,3,160,"sorghum",[4,1,3,2]],[4,70,8,190,"millet",[4,2,1,3]],[8,64,3,140,"sorghum",[1,2,3,4]],[3,75,7,205,"millet",[3,1,2,4]],[6,68,4,145,"sorghum",[3,4,2,1]],[4,72,6,230,"millet",[3,2,4,1]]];
E: L[ix];
m1: E[1]; p1: E[2]; m2: E[3]; p2: E[4]; fl: E[5]; pm: E[6];
nm: ["Akinyi","Kiprop","Wambui","Otieno","Nafula","Mwangi","Jepkosgei","Wekesa","Nyokabi","Abdi"][ix];
cc: (m1*p1+m2*p2)/(m1+m2);
mn: (p1+p2)/2;
tc: m1*p1+m2*p2;
/* diagnostics */
sp: p1+p2;
sw: (m2*p1+m1*p2)/(m1+m2);
mw: if m1>m2 then "more of the cheaper maize flour is used" else sconcat("more of the dearer ", fl, " flour is used");
OT: [sconcat(nm, " is right: a mixture always costs the mean of the two prices."),
  sconcat(nm, " is wrong: ", mw, ", so the cost per kilogram is nearer to the price of that flour."),
  sconcat(nm, " is wrong: the mixture costs the sum of the prices, Ksh ", string(sp), " a kilogram."),
  sconcat(nm, " is wrong: a mixture always costs the same per kilogram as the dearer flour.")];
opt1: makelist([pm[i], is(pm[i]=2), OT[pm[i]]], i, 1, 4);
]]></text>
  </questionvariables>
